#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186173277 :tutorial/content "To evaluate a large exponent, we first write out the power using multiplication signs as usual. Then, we calculate the product by splitting it into groups of two-digit multiplications, before calculating the resulting product.\n\nFor example, let's evaluate $2^4$.\n\nFirst, we write\n$4$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n2 \\times 2 = 4\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{2 \\times 2}_{\\large \\color{blue}4} \\times \\underbrace{2 \\times 2}_{\\large \\color{blue}4} = {\\color{blue}4} \\times {\\color{blue}4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we work out $4\\times 4$.\nSince\n\n$$\n4\\times 4=16\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $2^4=16$." :tutorial/id #uuid "4a00be57-d26e-53b8-9d16-7f4994f21077" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8955 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
